data: {"event_id":"01M2ST2883FZ9R77MGD3JM4V27","run_id":"8d3cdea1-99b6-2e60-1001-9fd13d044ed5","tenant_id":"0","session_id":"33cb3985-e16c-2f8f-3f45-80f6c62cb277","config_id":"f039a8d2-f0b7-5edf-4818-e5fdf3d38490","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:27:56.547201Z","seq":707,"source_event_id":"prt_27702cbeb97bf0a13e808be4","source_event_type":"message.part.updated","type":"run.tool_call_started","data":{"tool_call_id":"prt_27702cbeb97bf0a13e808be4","name":"bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/taskflow \u0026\u0026 gh pr create --title \"TF-104: Reject tasks with missing or blank title\" --body \"$(cat \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n## Root cause\n`src/app.js:35-39` created the task without any validation on the `title` field. A body with no `title` property (`{ status: 'todo' }`) resulted in `title` being `undefined`, and a body with whitespace-only title (`{ title: '   ' }`) stored a broken record — both returned 201.\n\n## Fix\nAdded a guard before the `store.create` call: if `title` is falsy or its trimmed value is empty, the endpoint returns 400 with `{ error: 'title is required' }`.\n\n## Verification\n`npm test` — 8 passed, 2 skipped (the 2 other skipped tests are for TF-101 and TF-102).\nEOF\n)\" 2\u003e\u00261","description":"Create pull request","timeout":30000}}}

